The big one for me is readability.

filter() # I know I'm filtering something.
!is.na <http://is.na>(x) #ah, I don't want NAs in column X

tet[!is.na <http://is.na/>(tet$x),]
# same thing really but you need to know to use `[` and "," in the right place.

But, it does the same thing so if you like the second version, you do you.

B

