xaringan is a very cool little package that allows you to create html slide presentations in RStudio. I just recently used it to give a talk at a conference, and I was pretty happy with the result (see slides here <https://ryanpeek.github.io/slides/20171025/2017_CA_SFS.html#1>). As long as you have internet connectivity, you can build in interactive slides, link to web content, and customize away. In addition you can print to pdf from your browser as a nice backup.

Take a look!

